  "review": {
    "id": "review-2026-09-28",
    "date": "2026-09-28",
    "title": "Hold the equity book; schedule a measured duration reduction",
    "type": "Forward review and pending paper instruction",
    "execute": null,
    "why": "The fixed-income thesis needs to recognise the changed policy regime. The Fed raised its target range to 3.75–4.00% on 16 September. Its projections put the end-2026 median rate at 4.1%. Reduce sensitivity to an inflation-led yield rise while retaining intermediate Treasuries as recession protection. This is a risk-budget choice, not a forecast that a policy hike automatically raises long yields.",
    "evidence": "Use completed 25 September closes for valuation. Review primary company releases and policy information available by 28 September. The cited releases predate this review, and the Fed release also predates the historical handover. This catches up a stale rationale; it is not portrayed as new news or as an earlier trade.",
    "alternative": "Hold the full duration exposure because tightening may already be priced and could weaken growth. A move entirely to short bonds would remove more recession protection. Choose a limited two-percentage-point shift rather than a full exit.",
    "risk": "Long yields can fall after a rate hike, causing the shorter book to lag. SHY remains exposed to USD/EUR and reinvestment rates. The illustrative duration assumptions are not current verified ETF analytics. There is no demonstrated pricing edge from the policy statement alone.",
    "invalidate": "Cancel or amend the instruction before execution if material new information reverses the inflation-versus-growth assessment. Reconsider adding duration after a sourced update on disinflation, labour-market deterioration and the actual Treasury curve. Do not infer an attractive entry yield from the old teaching model.",
    "implementation": "Pending, not filled: at the 29 September 2026 regular US closing reference, sell IEF equal to 2% of the portfolio's then pre-trade EUR NAV and buy the same EUR notional of SHY. Keep other units unchanged. Apply 25 bp to each leg, funded from existing EUR cash. Record all execution marks and EURUSD from the same valuation convention. If valid closes or sufficient cash/units are unavailable, leave the instruction unfilled. There is no automatic broker connection or scheduled execution; the next portfolio update must reconcile the fill before booking it.",
    "sources": [
      "fed-sep26",
      "sep-sep26",
      "cme-aug26",
      "rhm-h126",
      "su-h126",
      "ul-h126"
    ]
